Subject: [PATCH 02/12] fix(auth): verify Supabase JWT signatures - remove
 insecure decode fallback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

socialLogin() fell back to jwt.decode() (which ignores signatures) whenever
jwt.verify() threw, so any attacker could mint a token with an arbitrary email
claim and take over any account. This is an authentication-bypass /
account-takeover issue (critical).

- Added server/src/utils/supabaseAuth.ts with verifySupabaseJwt() that fails
  closed: missing secret or bad signature => 401. No decode fallback.
- socialLogin() now uses it; removed the hard-coded dev fallback secret from
  the verification path.
- Fixed AppError so subclasses keep their own prototype (Object.setPrototypeOf
  used AppError.prototype, breaking instanceof for UnauthorizedError and
  friends in the auth middleware).

Tests: server/src/utils/supabaseAuth.test.ts - accepts valid tokens; rejects
tokens signed with another secret, the legacy hard-coded secret, unsigned
tokens, and missing-secret configurations.

Run: cd server && npx jest src/utils/supabaseAuth.test.ts

